      "intro": "If your loved one is struggling with high heating and cooling bills, Indiana's Weatherization Assistance Program provides free energy efficiency upgrades to their home. The program covers weatherstripping, insulation installation, heating system tune-ups, water heater repairs, and air sealing, services that typically cost hundreds to thousands of dollars out of pocket.\n\nYour loved one qualifies if their household income is at or below 200% of the Federal Poverty Level, $28,660 for a single person or $38,680 for a couple in 2026. They're automatically eligible if they receive Energy Assistance Program (EAP), SSI, or TANF benefits. The program serves both homeowners and renters statewide, though renters need written landlord permission before any permanent installations.\n\nBecause 2026 program funds are limited and available on a first-come, first-served basis, early application is critical. After income verification, applicants join a waitlist until a Local Service Provider can schedule the 1-2 hour home assessment that determines which specific upgrades their home receives.",
