      "intro": "If your loved one is 55+ and unemployed with limited income, SCSEP provides paid job training in community service roles like child care aide, customer service, or health care worker. Your loved one earns minimum wage for about 20 hours per week while developing job-ready skills, with the goal of transitioning to permanent employment within 6 months.\n\nBecause this program combines income, training, and work experience, it helps older adults rebuild confidence and skills while earning money. Indiana has 1,059 available positions across multiple providers, but slots are limited and waitlists are common. Priority goes to veterans, adults 65+, those with disabilities, and rural residents.",
